      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/as-pure-t/q9-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"(−4 −8ℎ)2 + (ℎ+ 3)2 = 20 [M1] 64ℎ2 + 64ℎ+ 16 + ℎ2 + 6ℎ+ 9 = 20 65ℎ2 + 70ℎ+ 5 = 0, [A1] (13ℎ+ 1)(ℎ+ 1) = 0. The root ℎ= −1 gives 𝐴= (6, −1). The other gives ℎ= −1/13, 𝑘= −2 + 8/13 = −18/13. [A1] Now use 𝑃= (9, −7). The first equation becomes (𝑘−9)2+(ℎ+7)2 = 45; the radius equation is unchanged. Subtraction gives −14𝑘+ 8ℎ+ 92 = 0, or 4ℎ= 7𝑘−46. [M1] 16(𝑘−2)2 + (4ℎ+ 12)2 = 320 [M1] 16𝑘2 −64𝑘+ 64 + (7𝑘−34)2 = 320 65𝑘2 −540𝑘+ 900 = 0, 13𝑘2 −108𝑘+ 180 = 0 [A1] [A1] (13𝑘−30)(𝑘−6) = 0.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
